@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Layer 2.3 — proof submission (built; evidence-only)

skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4F46E5
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
}
autonumber

participant "Student phone\n(browser)" as Phone
participant "Express API" as API
participant "MongoDB" as DB

note over Phone
  The phone decoded a session, wave and key.
  The private P-256 key never leaves IndexedDB.
end note

Phone -> Phone: Build canonical message\nbioattend-proof:v1|session=…|wave=…|key=…|student=…
Phone -> Phone: Sign with the bound device key
Phone -> API: POST /api/v1/check-in-sessions/:id/proofs\n{ wave, key, signature }\n(cookie session)

API -> API: Origin guard · auth · student role\n60 proofs/min per student
API -> DB: Load session and check\nactive roster · approved binding\n· no pending device change
API -> API: Verify signature with the\nbound public key
API -> DB: Find existing proof for\n(session, student, wave)

alt Exact retry
  API --> Phone: 200\nduplicate: true · attendanceDecided: false
else New proof — active, fresh, current wave, key matches
  API -> DB: Insert evidence + signature +\nprotocol version (unique per student/wave)
  DB --> API: Stored, TTL ~24 h
  API --> Phone: 201\nrecorded: true · duplicate: false\nattendanceDecided: false
else Invalid, stale, wrong device or rate limited
  API --> Phone: 400 / 401 / 403 / 409 / 429
end

note over API, DB
  No score, attendance flag or ID round.
  The signed proof binds the submission to the bound account/device.
  It does not prove the phone was physically inside the room.
  A teacher may advance only after the current wave has
  at least one accepted proof; old keys are archived
  server-side and never returned to students.
end note

@enduml
